  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4x)=-1}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4x)=-1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\u2026}.\n$$",
